Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 00:25:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 060/106] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150-xiaomi-common: enable the
 PM6150 vibrator

pm6150.dtsi already declares the vibrator node (compatible
"qcom,pm6150-vib", "qcom,pmi632-vib") with a matching mainline driver
already built (pm8xxx-vibrator.c, CONFIG_INPUT_PM8XXX_VIBRATOR=m) - it
just ships status = "disabled" since not every pm6150 board has one
wired up. Downstream's sdmmagpie-common.dtsi confirms surya does
(qcom,vibrator@5300, 3.0V LDO, overdrive disabled), and no extra
properties are needed: the mainline driver doesn't parse the
downstream-only qcom,vib-ldo-volt-uv/qcom,disable-overdrive tunables,
just the register address already in the base dtsi.

Verified on real hardware: binds as input event "pm8xxx_vib_ffmemless"
(standard force-feedback API) and plays a rumble effect via a raw
FF_RUMBLE EVIOCSFF/EV_FF test, and via fbcli through the real Phosh
feedbackd stack.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
index 87ae63254..cc8f53a9f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
@@ -630,11 +630,16 @@ &pm6150_rtc {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&pm6150_vib {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &pm6150_typec {
 	vdd-vbus-supply = <&pm6150_vbus>;
 	vdd-pdphy-supply = <&vdda_usb_hs_3p1>;
 	status = "okay";
 
+
 	connector {
 		compatible = "usb-c-connector";
 
-- 
